hooks.prompt:
Prompt guard: no secrets or personal data in prompts. Hook input: $ARGUMENTS

Check only the prompt field. It fails if it contains a real-looking secret (an API key or token such as ghp_, github_pat_, sk-, AKIA, xoxb-, a private key block, a password inside a connection string) or a real-looking IBAN or national ID number. Mentioning secrets, .env files or passwords in general is fine. A prompt that starts with 'synthetic:' always passes.
Reply with JSON only: {"ok": true} if it passes, or {"ok": false, "reason": "Prompt not sent: it contains what looks like <what>. Remove it, or use synthetic data. If it was real, rotate it now."}

House style: no em-dashes in prose. Hook input: $ARGUMENTS

Look only at tool_input.file_path and the NEW text (tool_input.content, tool_input.new_string, or every edits[].new_string). It fails only if the path ends in .md, .mdx, .txt or .html and that new text contains an em-dash (U+2014). Anything else passes.
Reply with JSON only: {"ok": true} if it passes, or {"ok": false, "reason": "No em-dashes in prose. Rewrite those sentences with a colon, a comma, or two sentences."}
